"Let's get some practice validating arguments! This is really the beginning of *proof-writing* (the logical bones of it, anyway). The graphic of this world is the truth-table proof of the ***invalid*** argument that says: if §0 and §1 are true, then §2 must be true. See the highlighted row where the hypotheses are true, but the conclusion is false?"
