msgid "# **Sets & Set Connectives**\n"
"A **set** §0 is a collection of objects of some type §1 that satisfy a **membership predicate**, say §2. We often write sets by explicitly referring to the membership predicate. We call this **set-builder** notation. Here's how we would write the set of even integers in set-builder notation:\n"
