#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L02_equiv
msgid "# **Level 2: Contrapositives**\n"
"Let's use the laws of logic to prove that the ***Contrapositive*** of an implication is logically equivalent to the original implication."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `by_contra!`
#. §1: `by_contra`
#. §2: `push_neg`
#: Game.Levels.PfWorld.pf_docs
msgid "The tactic §0 is the same as §1 except that it applies §2 automically to the introduced hypothesis."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∨`
#. §1: $$ (P ∨ Q) ↔ (Q ∨ P) $$
#. §2: `Or_comm`
#. §3: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|cc||cc|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & P ∨ Q & Q ∨ P  \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T & T \\
#.   T & F & T & T \\
#.   F & T & T & T \\
#.   F & F & F & F \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
msgid "This is the **Commutative Law** for §0. It says that\n"
"§1\n"
"The proof of §2 follows from the truth-table below:\n"
"§3"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h₁`
#. §1: ```
#. obtain h₃ := h₁ h₂
#. ```
#. §2: `a`
#. §3: `h₁ : a ∈ A`
#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.L01_set
msgid "See how the hypothesis §0 is now rewritten according to the definition? Now try\n"
"§1\n"
"**Note:** we didn't have to specify the value §2! This was inferred from §3.\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.RelationWorld.RelationWorldExamples.relation_example4
msgid "Practice with inverses."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P`
#. §1: `¬ Q`
#. §2: `R`
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.EquivWorld_eg.L02_equiv
msgid "### **💡 Pro-tip**\n"
"The result of this level tells you that if you want to prove and if-then statement where the conclusion is a disjunction, then you may do so by... **assuming** that §0 and §1 are true, and then showing that §2 must follow."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `R`
#. §1: `u`
#. §2: `isMaximal R b`
#. §3: `b`
#. §4: `u`
#. §5: `b`
#. §6: `B`
#. §7: `u`
#. §8: `isMaximal R b B`
#: Game.Levels.RelationWorld.Relation_docs
msgid "If §0 is a relation on §1, §2 means that §3 is a maximal element of §4.\n"
"\n"
"If we want to specify that §5 is a maximal element of a subset §6 of §7, write §8."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L02_arg
